        'A model claims 98% accuracy on service failures. The dataset has 2% failures, repeated devices across splits and a repair-code feature written after failure. An always-no-failure rule also gets 98%. These three issues require separate fixes: a useful metric, a deployment-matched split and removal of future information.',
